<languages/>
[https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%95%D7%99%D7%A7%D7%99%D7%A4%D7%93%D7%99%D7%94:%D7%97%D7%A9%D7%99%D7%91%D7%95%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%A0%D7%A6%D7%99%D7%A7%D7%9C%D7%95%D7%A4%D7%93%D7%99%D7%AA חשיבות אנציקלופדית] היא הרעיון של איך לקבוע אילו סוגי תוכן ראויים להיכלל בוויקי. אמנם כבר קיימים כללים המסדירים את [[Special:MyLanguage/VRCWiki:Guidelines#Type_of_permitted_content|סוגי התוכן המותרים]] בוויקי הזה בכללותו, אך הנחיות החשיבות האנציקלופדית חלות בתוך הקטגוריות האלה כדי להסדיר דפים ספציפיים ואת הכללתם.

החשיבות האנציקלופדית בוויקי של VRChat קובעת אם נושא ראוי לדף משלו. החשיבות האנציקלופדית היא עיקרון מרכזי שמבטיח שהתוכן בוויקי של VRChat נשאר ניתן לאימות, רלוונטי ומשמעותי בקהילת VRChat. 

אין בכך ערובה שנושא יטופל בהכרח כדף נפרד ועצמאי. עורכים רשאים לפעול לפי שיקול דעתם כדי למזג או לקבץ שני נושאים קשורים או יותר לדף אחד. ההנחיות האלה רק מתוות עד כמה נושא מתאים לדף משלו או לרשימה משלו. הן אינן מגבילות את התוכן של דף או של רשימה.
== קריטריונים לחשיבות אנציקלופדית של עולמות ==
עולם ב-VRChat נחשב חשוב מספיק כדי להצדיק דף במרחב השמות Main אם הוא עומד באחד מהקריטריונים הבאים:

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* [[List of worlds created by VRChat|Official VRChat worlds]].
* Worlds featured by VRChat (Spotlight and special event categories such as VKet and Jams).
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
A VRChat world is considered notable enough to warrant an article in the Community Namespace if it meets one of the following criteria:
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* World that have had notable independent external coverage by reliable sources, such as [[Special:MyLanguage/Community:Treehouse in the Shade|Treehouse in the Shade]].
* Worlds that meet all of the following statistical criteria:
** Worlds that have made it out of Community Labs AND
** Have at least 10,000 visits or 1,000 favorites.
</div>
<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Exclusions ===
The following types of worlds are not allowed on the VRChat Wiki, even if they meet the above criteria:
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* Worlds which violate VRChat's Terms of Service and Community Guidelines.
* Worlds that prominently or excessively feature the following concepts. The consistency in which these exclusions apply will vary based on context. If unsure, always refer to VRChat's Terms of Service and Community Guidelines.
** Sexual content and nudity
** Hateful and offensive content
** Drug use
</div>
<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Notability criteria for avatars==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Avatar pages should only be created for the following types of avatars:
* Official VRChat avatars
* Avatars part of the [[Public Avatars|Public Avatar Row]]
* Avatars, otherwise featured by VRChat
* Notable avatars made by the community
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
For a newly created Avatar page, it should be obvious or made obvious, that such Avatar or Avatar Type is notable enough. Therefore it is advised to create a [[VRCWiki:How to Contribute#Discussion Page|Discussion page]] right after a new Avatar page has been created with a note as for why the page was made. This helps to evaluate notability. Pages where this cannot be easily ascertained with may be deleted.
</div>
<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
== General notability guidelines ==
For other types of content and subjects, the following guidelines apply to determine notability:
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* A subject should have received significant coverage in reliable sources that are independent of the subject.
* The coverage should be more than trivial or incidental. It should provide meaningful insight into the subject.
* Content should be verifiable and should maintain a [[Special:MyLanguage/VRCWiki:Neutral point of view|Neutral Point of View]] (NPOV).
</div>
<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
== Content quality ==
All content must be verifiable if possible and contributors should use common sense. Avoid advertising and use neutral language. The goal is to inform, not to promote.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
By adhering to these guidelines, we ensure that the VRChat Wiki remains a reliable and valuable resource for the VRChat community.
</div>
